  "question": {
    "text": "In normal adjustment, for a refracting telescope, the distance between objective and eye piece is 30 cm . The focal length of the objective, when the angular magnification of the telescope is 2 , will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "20 cm",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "30 cm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "10 cm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "15 cm",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because \\mathrm{f}_0+\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{e}}=30$\nAnd magnification, $\\mathrm{m}=\\frac{\\mathrm{f}_0}{\\mathrm{f}_e}$\n$2=\\frac{\\mathrm{f}_0}{\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{e}}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}_0=2 \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{e}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}_0+\\frac{\\mathrm{f}_0}{2}=30 \\therefore \\mathrm{f}_0=20cm$"
  }
}